    {
      "id": "207:1590",
      "name": "06 · How it works (Melo's homepage draft, 29 Oct 2026; Figma pending)",
      "text": [
        [
          "draft:how/title",
          "Know what happened?\nGet paid to report it."
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/1",
          "Every Augur Lituus answer has REP staked behind it. Be right and you're paid. Be wrong and you lose your stake."
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/2",
          "1"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/3",
          "Ask"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/4",
          "Pay a fee in REP"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/5",
          "2"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/6",
          "Report"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/7",
          "Stake on an answer"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/8",
          "3"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/9",
          "Challenge"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/10",
          "Back another answer"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/11",
          "4"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/12",
          "Get paid"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/13",
          "If your answer holds"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/14",
          "Anyone can ask."
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/15",
          "A fee funds the reward."
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/16",
          "The reward grows until someone reports what happened."
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/17",
          "Ask"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/18",
          "Say someone asks, \"Has room-temperature superconductivity been independently demonstrated at ambient pressure?\" They set the rules for judging it and pay a fee in REP. Part of it pays whoever first backs the right answer; the rest is burned. In this example, the fee is"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/19",
          "15 REP."
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/20",
          "Report"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/21",
          "Anyone can report. Here, someone reports"
        ],
        [
          "I207:1597;145:261",
          "YES"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/22",
          "and stakes"
        ],
        [
          "I207:1597;145:270",
          "15 REP"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/23",
          "on it, the same as the fee."
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/24",
          "Challenge"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/25",
          "You think the reporter is wrong, so you challenge with"
        ],
        [
          "I207:1597;145:263",
          "NO"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/26",
          "and stake"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/27",
          "30 REP"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/28",
          "on it, double theirs. The time to challenge starts again, and now anyone can challenge you."
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/29",
          "Get paid"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/30",
          "No one challenges you in time, so the final answer is"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/31",
          "NO. You get your 30 REP back, plus"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/32",
          "12 REP"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/33",
          "from the reporter's stake, plus"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/34",
          "the reward. The other 3 REP of their stake is burned."
        ],
        [
          "draft:how/holder",
          "Holding REP?"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/35",
          "How REP works"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/36",
          "Earn REP"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/37",
          "Report or challenge when you know what happened, and get paid in REP when your answer holds."
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/38",
          "Stay in the loop"
        ],
        [
          "melo:how/39",
          "Holding is mostly hands-off. If a fork ever starts, there's a window to move your REP to the answer you believe in."
        ]
      ]
    },
